  "result": "The subcommand `default_map` bug is fixed, and the full test suite passes (1908 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/click/core.py:392`: a child context now receives `parent.default_map.get(info_name)` instead of the entire parent map. This gives each subcommand its own section, and a missing entry resolves to `None`.\n- `tests/test_defaults.py`: added two tests at the end of the file:\n  - `test_default_map_subcommand` checks that `default_map={\"sub\": {...}}` applies to `sub`, and that an entry for a different subcommand doesn't.\n  - `test_default_map_nested_subcommand` checks that `{\"group\": {\"sub\": {...}}}` applies to `group sub`.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the unfixed code to confirm they fail there. By reading the code, without the fix `sub` would look up `name` in the parent map, miss it, and get `original`, so the assertions would fail.\n\nI haven't committed anything. Say if you want a commit, and I'll use the attribution line from the reminder.",
